course: dictionary
lesson: 7801
title: Quart: a measure and a saying
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A quart is a unit for measuring liquids, such as milk or juice. Two pints make one quart, and four quarts make one gallon.
explain: Quart is mostly used in the USA. Context helps: «Milk and ice cream in the USA often come in quart cartons» tells you a quart is a container-sized amount of liquid, not a tiny drop.
explain: A US quart is a little under a litre, but an old British quart was bigger, about 1.14 litres, because British pints were bigger. So check the text to see which country it means.
explain: Quart also appears in a UK saying, «You can't fit a quart into a pint pot», which means you cannot fit too much into too small a space. The French «cinq heures moins le quart» means quarter to five, because le quart means a quarter.
fact: A quart is a unit for measuring liquids.
fact: 2 pints = 1 quart, and 4 quarts = 1 gallon.
fact: A US quart is about 0.95 litres; an old British quart was about 1.14 litres.
fact: «You can't fit a quart into a pint pot» means you cannot fit too much into too small a space.
fact: «Cinq heures moins le quart» is French for quarter to five; moins means minus.
exercise: What is a quart? | A kind of bread | *A unit for measuring liquids | A small coin | A kind of tree
exercise: How many pints make one quart? | *2 | 3 | 4 | 1
exercise: «You can't fit a quart into a pint pot» means? | *You cannot fit too much into too small a space | A quart is cheaper than a pint | A pint pot is too expensive
test: How many quarts make one gallon? | *4 | 8 | 2 | 16
test: About how many litres is a US quart? | About 0.095 litres | About 9.5 litres | About 100 litres | *About 0.95 litres
exam: Which is the best size for an old British quart? | About 11 litres | About 0.2 litres | *About 1.14 litres
